edhat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"9.1","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"9.1"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"CRITICAL","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"critical"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-07-01T13:49:27.306Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-01t13:49:27.306z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-07-15T01:18:20.267Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-15t01:18:20.267z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"description","object":"A vulnerability has been identified in the Feast Feature Server\u2019s `/save-document` endpoint that allows an unauthenticated remote attacker to write arbitrary JSON files to the server's filesystem. Although the system attempts to restrict file locations, these protections can be bypassed, enabling an attacker to overwrite vital application configurations or startup scripts. Because this flaw requires no credentials or special privileges, any attacker with network access to the server can potentially compromise the integrity of the system. This could lead to unauthorized system modifications, denial of service through disk exhaustion, or potential remote code execution.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a vulnerability has been identified in the feast feature server\u2019s `/save-document` endpoint that allows an unauthenticated remote attacker to write arbitrary json files to the server's filesystem. although the system attempts to restrict file locations, these protections can be bypassed, enabling an attacker to overwrite vital application configurations or startup scripts. because this flaw requires no credentials or special privileges, any attacker with network access to the server can potentially compromise the integrity of the system. this could lead to unauthorized system modifications, denial of service through disk exhaustion, or potential remote code execution."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"product","object":"Feast Feature Server","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"feast feature server"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI)","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat openshift ai (rhoai)"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-862","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-862"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"vendor","object":"Feast","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"feast"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23537","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"assigner","object":"redhat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"redhat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"cvss-base-score","object":"7.5","source":"cve","object_type":"number","object_canonical":"7.5"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"cvss-severity","object":"HIGH","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"high"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-07-16T00:10:50.170Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-16t00:10:50.170z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-07-16T13:58:04.495Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-07-16t13:58:04.495z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"description","object":"A vulnerability was identified in the Feast Feature Server's `/ws/chat` endpoint that allows remote attackers to establish persistent WebSocket connections without any authentication. By opening a large number of simultaneous connections, an attacker can exhaust server resources\u2014such as memory, CPU, and file descriptors\u2014leading to a complete denial of service for legitimate users.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a vulnerability was identified in the feast feature server's `/ws/chat` endpoint that allows remote attackers to establish persistent websocket connections without any authentication. by opening a large number of simultaneous connections, an attacker can exhaust server resources\u2014such as memory, cpu, and file descriptors\u2014leading to a complete denial of service for legitimate users."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"product","object":"Feast Feature Server","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"feast feature server"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI)","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat openshift ai (rhoai)"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-770","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-770"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"vendor","object":"Feast","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"feast"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56210","predicate":"affects-cpe","object"