d of approximately 40,728 bytes when computing a layer context array index. An attacker who can influence SVC encoder parameters in a network-facing service could exploit this for information disclosure (heap content leak) or denial of service (segmentation fault from hitting unmapped memory).","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a heap-buffer-overflow read vulnerability was found in libaom, the reference av1 codec implementation. a missing bounds check in the svc (scalable video coding) layer id control function allows setting a spatial_layer_id exceeding the configured number of layers. this causes an out-of-bounds heap read of approximately 40,728 bytes when computing a layer context array index. an attacker who can influence svc encoder parameters in a network-facing service could exploit this for information disclosure (heap content leak) or denial of service (segmentation fault from hitting unmapped memory)."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56210","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Hardened Images","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat hardened images"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56210","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat AI Inference Server","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ai inference server"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56210","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 10"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56210","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56210","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux AI (RHEL AI) 3","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux ai (rhel ai) 3"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56210","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI)","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"r